05A6A2             1122*   ; Normalize the mutable camera position into the manager's proposed axial
05A6A2             1123*   ; origin.  IX is opaque to the manager but is the fixture's p3d camera state
05A6A2             1124*   ; here.  The closed hex has Pingo-local corners
05A6A2             1125*   ;
05A6A2             1126*   ;   (x,z) = (0,-5120),(4400,-2560),(4400,2560),
05A6A2             1127*   ;           (0,5120),(-4400,2560),(-4400,-2560).
05A6A2             1128*   ;
05A6A2             1129*   ; Hence the sloped half-plane witness is exactly
05A6A2             1130*   ;
05A6A2             1131*   ;   1024*abs(x) + 1760*abs(z) <= 9,011,200.
05A6A2             1132*   ;
05A6A2             1133*   ; Both (0,5120) and (4400,2560) evaluate to 9,011,200.  Rebase does not occur
05A6A2             1134*   ; on that ownership boundary.  The current origin retains a fixed 256-count
05A6A2             1135*   ; (16 m) outward band.  For each sloped edge the exact integer witness is
05A6A2             1136*   ;
05A6A2             1137*   ;   round(256*sqrt(1024^2+1760^2)) = 521,271,
05A6A2             1138*   ;   retained half-plane RHS = 9,532,471.
05A6A2             1139*   ;
05A6A2             1140*   ; The expanded vertical and tip quick bounds are respectively 4,656 and
05A6A2             1141*   ; 5,376 counts.  Exact outer-limit ties retain the current origin; the first
05A6A2             1142*   ; integer beyond a limit selects a neighbor.  The branch order below gives
05A6A2             1143*   ; corners a deterministic vertical-before-sloped tie rule.  After a rebase,
05A6A2             1144*   ; applying the same expanded hex around the new origin supplies the symmetric
05A6A2             1145*   ; deadband, so boundary jitter cannot immediately select the old origin.
05A6A2             1146*   ; Axis checks reduce arbitrarily displaced signed-word inputs before the
05A6A2             1147*   ; multiplication, so each unsigned product and sum fits in 24 bits.
